    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/agent-handoff.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "One task, two agents, one human between them",
      "prov:value": "## Why this exists: bean `mac1`, 2026-10-02\n\nThe cloud session could restore and verify an FHIR AST cache, but it could not\nbuild one, because `packages.fhir.org` was blocked. It wrote bean `mac1` for a\nlocal agent on the owner's Mac: re-seed two caches, done when `verify` passes\non a fresh clone. The handoff went wrong in five ways, and all five were\nvisible only from outside:\n\n| what happened | the rule it breaks |\n|---|---|\n| the executor worked in another checkout (`folio-assistant-backup`) and created **its own** bean, so two files on one branch now carry the id `mac1` | §1, claim the handed bean and never create one |\n| the bean said \"STOP and report the counts\" without saying where, so the coordinator had to add a channel mid-flight, and the owner asked *\"hopefully your bean told where to coordinate\"* | §2, the report channel is in the bean from the start |\n| one cache was seeded from `5891a22` while the IG's `main` was `e151a4d`, because the executor's checkout was behind | §4, pin the inputs and check them first |\n| the executor closed `mac1` on its own build log, and `verify` on a fresh clone failed for **both** caches | §5, the verifier closes |\n| the coordinator \"approved\" a `--force` in a PR comment that the bean itself forbade | §6, only the owner grants an exception |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mac1",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/agent-handoff.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. One bean, one writer, and the receiver claims it",
      "prov:value": "That is a **stop-and-report**, not a cue to recreate\nthe bean: a fresh `beans create` mints a new id, or, as with `mac1`, a second\nfile under an id someone typed by hand, and now two beans answer one question.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mac1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/agent-handoff.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "3. One sentence to paste, and a brief inside the bean",
      "prov:value": "A paste that carries\nthe instructions is long, unversioned and impossible to correct. A paste that\ncarries less (\"do bean `mac1`, report on #1816\") leaves the executor asking\nwhich branch, as the owner had to ask on 2026-10-02.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mac1",
        "#1816",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/agent-handoff.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "3. One sentence to paste, and a brief inside the bean",
      "prov:value": "the exact commands, with a test that FAILS in the wrong checkout, ending in `beans:claim` | naming the checkout is not enough: `mac1`'s executor ran from `-backup` in all three attempts |\n| the task in two or three sentences, and why the last attempt failed | so the executor knows what the pins guard against |\n| REPORT: where, and the line formats | §2 |\n| STOP AND REPORT IF | the bean's `## Fails if` |\n| LIMITS | §6, plus \"never create or edit any other bean\" |\n| FINISH: evidence, `ready-to-close`, commit only this bean, final report line | §5 |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mac1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/agent-handoff.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "4. Pin the inputs, and check them before acting",
      "prov:value": "A long-lived checkout carries untracked files,\nlocal edits and line-ending conversions that a clean clone does not, and the\nconsumer will have a clean clone. In `mac1`, the trust IG's recorded digest\n(`e9eb867e…`) matched nothing a clean clone of the same commit computes\n(`c1023d82…`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mac1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/agent-handoff.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "5. The executor's measurement is evidence, not the close",
      "prov:value": "A build log saying \"678 resources, 671 edges\" is the executor's view of its\nown tree. `mac1`'s criterion was `verify` on a fresh clone, and it failed\nwhile the log read clean.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mac1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/agent-handoff.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "5. The executor's measurement is evidence, not the close",
      "prov:value": "**The executor's own check runs on an untouched copy, not on the tree it\nbuilt in.** A build leaves its own files behind, so a check run where the\nwork happened agrees with itself whether or not the work is right. In `mac1`\nattempt 2 the executor's `verify` read `valid` in its build clone, and the\nverifier's read `stale-inputs` on untouched clones for both caches. So the\nbean's local-check step names a **second** copy: a new clone, a clean\ncontainer, the published artefact.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mac1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/agent-handoff.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "7. When the executor fails",
      "prov:value": "created a bean, wrote another bean, pushed outside the boundaries | an unexpected file or ref | a duplicate bean is re-identified and `scrapped` with a pointer, never deleted (`mac1` → `8ao5`); a stray push is **reported to the owner**, never reverted by the coordinator ([`deletion-requires-confirmation`](../../../skills/conduct/conduct-core/deletion-requires-confirmation.md)) |\n| **partial**: some items done | per-item lines | per-item evidence; the bean stays open until every item verifies |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mac1",
        "bean 8ao5"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
